Classical Electromagnetism — Richard Fitzpatrick (@em-fitzpatrick: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_7NH7AZZH3NZ2FHJ4K5VBT49F6H
Richard Fitzpatrick, University of Texas at Austin. [Online textbook](https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/jk1/Electromagnetism/index.html) · [Complete author-hosted PDF](https://farside.ph.utexas.edu/teaching/jk1/Electromagnetism.pdf).

Read this full advanced companion, with particular sustained study of boundary-value problems, Green functions, angular expansions, electromagnetic matter, waves, radiation and relativity. Derive the intermediate steps and compare conventions with Tong and the engineering books.

The author-hosted PDF inspected on 29 October 2026 has 307 file pages. Its title and contents were checked; a publication year or blanket CC licence is not inferred from the hosting date. This is a distinct work/version from the author's separately published commercial books. Free reading is available; preserve copyright and component notices. No book or figures are stored in this repository.

